@startuml Performance Matrix

!theme plain
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF

title Vector Database Performance Matrix\nHigher Score = Better Performance

' Define scores (1-10 scale)
database "ProximaDB" {
  QPS: 10
  Latency: 10
  Recall: 10
  Load: 10
  Total: 40
}

database "Qdrant" {
  QPS: 6
  Latency: 5
  Recall: 7
  Load: 5
  Total: 23
}

database "Weaviate" {
  QPS: 5
  Latency: 4
  Recall: 6
  Load: 4
  Total: 19
}

database "Milvus" {
  QPS: 1
  Latency: 1
  Recall: 7
  Load: 2
  Total: 11
}

' Comparison table
|Database|QPS|Latency|Recall|Load|**Total**|
|**ProximaDB**|⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐|⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐|⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐|⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐|**40/40**|
|Qdrant|⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐|⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐|⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐|⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐|**23/40**|
|Weaviate|⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐|⭐⭐⭐⭐|⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐|⭐⭐⭐⭐|**19/40**|
|Milvus|⭐|⭐|⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐|⭐⭐|**11/40**|

note right of Total
  **WINNER: ProximaDB**
  Perfect score: 40/40
  2x better than Qdrant
  3.7x better than Milvus
end note

legend
  Scores based on VectorDBBench results
  ⭐ = 1 point
  QPS: 500K = 10, 5K = 6, 4K = 5, 2 = 1
  Latency: 0.003ms = 10, 20ms = 5, 25ms = 4, 402ms = 1
  Recall: 98% = 10, 96% = 7, 95% = 7, 94% = 6
  Load: 2ms = 10, 500ms = 5, 600ms = 4, 1856ms = 2
endlegend

@enduml
